# mise-tasks

Each task is a separate executable file. The file name is the task name: `mise run clone` runs `mise-tasks/clone`, and `mise run api:test` runs `mise-tasks/api/test`.

## Tasks

| File | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `setup` | `hk install --mise`, `kit:install` when sdd-kit is missing, `mise lock` when `mise.lock` is missing, `add-repo` when `repos.toml` is empty, `clone`, then each clone's `install` |
| `add-repo` | `node scripts/repos.mjs add`: asks for repositories, appends them to `repos.toml`, runs `repos:sync`, offers to clone |
| `repos/sync`, `repos/check` | Regenerate, or check, everything that lists the repositories ([../docs/agents/tooling.md](../docs/agents/tooling.md)) |
| `clone` | Clones the missing clones from `[bootstrap.repos]` on their rest branch, leaves existing clones alone |
| `pull` | `git pull --rebase --autostash` in the meta-repository and each clone on its branch, lists failures and branches without upstream |
| `status` | Branch and number of changed files in each clone, a missing clone is marked `missing` |
| `check` | A step per clone (`<name>:check`), `code-rules`, `repos` and a result table |
| `lint` | `rumdl`, `typos`, `agnix` and `scripts/check-agent-files.sh` |
| `test` | Meta-repository tests from `tests/` |
| `kit/install`, `kit/update` | Install or update sdd-kit through `scripts/kit.sh` |
| `<name>/test`, `<name>/check`, `<name>/run`, `<name>/install` | A clone's own commands, created as stubs by `repos:sync` |

Shared clone helpers live in `scripts/clones.sh`: the clone list from `[bootstrap.repos]`, the repository names from `repos.toml`, a check that a clone exists and the stub ending `not_configured`.

## A clone's tasks

`mise run repos:sync` creates `mise-tasks/<name>/{test,check,run,install}` for a new repository. Each stub changes into the clone and fails with "command not configured yet". Replace its last line with the clone's own command and delete the `# repos:stub` comment, for example:

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
#MISE description="api: tests, optionally one test file (npm test in repos/api)"
set -euo pipefail
source "$MISE_CONFIG_ROOT/scripts/clones.sh"
require_clone repos/api
cd repos/api
exec npm test -- "$@"
```

A clone may need more tasks, for example a background worker; add them to its folder the same way. `mise run repos:sync` lists every extra task in the clone's command table in `AGENTS.md`, with the text of its `#MISE description="<name>: <text>"` line.

## Adding a task

Create a file with the shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, a `#MISE description="..."` line and the executable bit (`chmod +x`). Arguments are declared with `#USAGE arg "<name>"` lines, and the value arrives in the `usage_<name>` variable. The task runs with the meta-repository root as its working directory. A clone task with the same name overrides the meta-repository task when `mise run` is called inside the clone.

The `mise-tasks` hook in `hk.pkl` checks the syntax on commit. Tests in `tests/` check the tasks' behaviour.
